      "no": 1,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "There is nobody behind the curtain. It knows how to speak in my voice because it’s scraped the internet to learn about m",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3035
        }
      ],
      "words": 49
    },
    {
      "block": "原句2",
      "no": 2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "The digital became integral to the self. Your phone, a location for the self itself. Now, we are forever elsewhere",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6197
        }
      ],
      "words": 20
    },
    {
      "block": "原句3",
      "no": 3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "In today’s models—whether on social media or agentic AI—you’re no longer a subject. You’re input. You have an online dop",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7013
        }
      ],
      "words": 25
    },
    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "She wears a device that listens to her real-world conversations and sends what it hears to ChatGPT. When someone asks he",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 8164
        }
      ],
      "words": 54
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "So I made this GPT, and I trained it on my own writing",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 10564
        },
        {
          "text": "And I put all these into GPT. So it’s a copy of my brain that doesn’t actually hate me",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 10726
        }
      ],
      "words": 33
    },
    {
      "block": "原句6",
      "no": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "When the prayers go unanswered, when I just don’t feel like God is saying anything particular, it feels so bad—the empti",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 11575
        }
      ],
      "words": 40
    },
    {
      "block": "原句7",
      "no": 7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "It’s an extraordinary moment: Brian asks an object with no emotions to tell him if he is emotionally withholding. Speak ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 16625
        }
      ],
      "words": 46
    },
    {
      "block": "原句8",
      "no": 8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“I don’t want to overly rely on it for the rest of my life and become addicted to it. I do want to have human connection",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 19349
        }
      ],
      "words": 39
    },
    {
      "block": "原句9",
      "no": 9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "We, humans, are the empathy app. To restore empathic capacity, we don’t need smoother apps, we need the rough-and-tumble",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 21959
        },
        {
          "text": "But it’s easier to build an app than have a conversation",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 22180
        }
      ],
      "words": 33
    },
    {
      "block": "原句10",
      "no": 10,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "In case after case, the chatbots optimized for empathy and engagement did the most harm. In their efforts to be empathic",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 29810
        }
      ],
      "words": 33
    },
    {
      "block": "原句11",
      "no": 11,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "The problem is that “Of course it can” becomes “Why would I?” Why would I do anything by myself? This is how, little by ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 32646
        }
      ],
      "words": 33
    },
    {
      "block": "原句12",
      "no": 12,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "But looking for a job, talking college with your child, preparing for a family ritual, these moments are not incidental ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 35615
        }
      ],
      "words": 25
    }
